        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e08328a7-a1f3-5446-8102-526681ee743b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Glenn Quagmire, Seth MacFarlane, Brian Griffin, Cheryl Tiegs\n- Roles: creator, voice actor, actress\n- Works: Family Guy, Ted, Ted 2, A Million Ways to Die in the West, Tiegs for Two\n- Concepts: 1950s party-animal clichés, rat-pack era\n\nFacts:\n- Seth MacFarlane wrote, directed, and starred in the film \"Ted\" in 2012.\n- Seth MacFarlane wrote, directed, and starred in the film \"A Million Ways to Die in the West\" in 2014.\n- Seth MacFarlane wrote, directed, and starred in the film \"Ted 2\" in 2015.\n- Seth MacFarlane, the creator and voice actor of Family Guy, described Glenn Quagmire as \"an appalling human being who is still caught in the rat-pack era\" and based the character on anachronistic 1950s party-animal clichés.\n- In the episode \"Tiegs for Two,\" Brian Griffin fails again at getting a date and seeks advice from Glenn Quagmire.\n- In the episode \"Tiegs for Two,\" Glenn Quagmire pursues his ex-lover, actress Cheryl Tiegs.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
